 finite present form.","C":"Two distinct people joined by **and** form a plural subject.","D":"The subject names two separate people, not one unit."}}},{"id":"5fefaa1b-da00-551b-a139-598f90c4b272","topicSlug":"agreement-advanced","level":"B2","prompt":"“Each of the people assigned to repair the rowing boat ____ a copy of the instructions.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"has"},{"id":"B","text":"have"},{"id":"C","text":"having"},{"id":"D","text":"to have"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The phrase **each of** selects members individually and takes a singular verb.","explanation":"The subject head **each** is singular, so use **has**.","keywords":["each-of-agreement"],"skill":"each-of-agreement","contextKey":"agreement-advanced-50","fingerprint":"0e32d717827f0878245bd209ea731c9ae32644d1c79a623b58cc475cc653c539","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-agreement"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The phrase **each of** selects members individually and takes a singular verb.","The subject head **each** is singular, so use **has**.","Choose **has**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The subject head **each** is singular, so use **has**.","B":"The plural people is inside an of phrase; each controls agreement.","C":"Having alone is not a finite verb.","D":"An infinitive cannot be the finite predicate here."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Find the head of a subject phrase and handle indefinite pronouns, quantities and collective nouns carefully.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that form is useful. Read each section with both questions in mind. The examples make one contrast at a time, while the practice mixes the skills so that you learn to recognise the pattern yourself."],"rules":[{"title":"The head controls agreement","explanation":"A subject can contain another noun inside a prepositional phrase. In ordinary agreement, the **head of the subject phrase** controls the verb, not the nearest noun. The box of tools is singular because box is the head.","pattern":"The **list** of names **is** ready.","commonMistakes":["The list of names are ready incorrectly lets the nearby plural names control agreement."],"examples":["“The list of tasks needed to prepare the visitor guide **is** ready.”","“The list of tasks needed to restore the old portrait **is** ready.”"],"skill":"form"},{"title":"Indefinite pronouns","explanation":"Everyone, someone, anybody and each normally take singular verb agreement. They can still be referred back to with singular they. Each of the students is ready combines singular each with a plural noun inside an of phrase.","pattern":"**Everyone is** ready; **they** have a ticket.","commonMistakes":["Singular they does not change the agreement of everyone itself to plural."],"examples":["“Everyone who can prepare the visitor guide **is** welcome.”","“Everyone who can restore the old portrait **is** welcome.”"],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Coordinated subjects and quantities","explanation":"Two separate subjects joined by and normally take a plural verb. A combined dish, title or single measured amount can be treated as one unit. Percentages and fractions often take agreement from what is being measured.","pattern":"The guide and the driver **are** here. / Ten pounds **is** enough.","commonMistakes":["Agreement with quantities depends on meaning: ten pounds is a price, but the coins are separate objects."],"examples":["“The guide and the assistant **are** ready to prepare the visitor guide.”","“The guide and the assistant **are** ready to restore the old portrait.”"],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Collective nouns and variation","explanation":"A team or committee may take singular agreement when treated as one unit. British English also commonly uses plural agreement when its members are in focus; American English more often favours singular. Keep pronoun choices and viewpoint consistent.","pattern":"The team **is** united. / The team **are** arguing among themselves.","commonMistakes":["Do not label every plural collective agreement wrong without specifying variety and intended meaning."],"examples":["“Each of the people assigned to prepare the visitor guide **has** a copy of the instructions.”","“Each of the people assigned to restore the old portrait **has** a copy of the instructions.”"],"skill":"application"}],"recap":["The **list** of names **is** ready.","**Everyone is** ready; **they** have a ticket.","The guide and the driver **are** here. / Ten pounds **is** enough.","The team **is** united. / The team **are** arguing among themselves."]},"stage":"5 · Complex sentences","prerequisites":["punctuation-clauses"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
